 "hints": [
  "The starter stores only the first plane. You need both planes, element by element.",
  "Adding along the leading axis is exactly what `reduce` does: `pop=1` folds away axis 0 and keeps the 3x4.",
  "Replace the `index` with `reduce %t op=add pop=1`. The result is shape `(3, 4)`; reshape it to `[12]` before the store."
 ],
 "explain": "`reduce %t op=add pop=1` folds away the leading axis, so each output element is `x[0][j][k] + x[1][j][k]`, with i32 wraparound as always (`INT_MAX + 1` is `INT_MIN`). Memory is flat, so the 3x4 result is reshaped to `[12]` for the store; row-major order makes that free."
}